File Handling:

Python can read this file and process its content.
--------------------------------------------------
|Open()|

# opening a file.

file = open("personal_loan.txt", "r")
-----------------------------

|close()|

When Python opens a file, it creates a resource.
-----------------------------------------------
|With open()|

# python automatically closes the file after leaving the with block.

with open("personal_loan.txt", "r") as file:
    content = file.read()
print(content)

--------------------------------------------------
| "r" |

# read a file/ read mode.

file = open("personal_loan.txt", "r")
content = file.read()
print(content)
file.close()
----------------------------------------------------------------------
|File modes|

Mode	| Meaning
----------------
"r"   |	Read
"w"   |	Write
"a"	  |Append
"x"	  |Create new file
-----------------------------------------------------------
|Read Mode — "r"|

try:
    with open("data.txt", "r") as file:
        content = file.read()
    print(content)

except FileNotFoundError:
    print("File not found")

#If the file doesn't exist, Python raises: FileNotFoundError:
------------------------------------------------------------------
|Write Mode — "w"|

-> If the file doesn't exist, Python creates it.
-> If it already exists, "w" overwrites the existing content.

with open("customer.txt", "w") as file:
    file.write("Customer Name: Priya")
-------------------------------------------------
|Append Mode — "a"|

--> If you want to add content without deleting existing content:

with open("customer.txt", "a") as file:
    file.write("\nAccount Type: Savings")

------------------------------------------------------------
|Reading Line by Line|

with open("loan.txt", "r") as file:

    for line in file:
        print(line)

-> This reads the file one line at a time.
-------------------------------------------------
|read() vs readline() vs readlines()|

-> read()
Reads the entire file.
content = file.read()

-> readline()
Reads one line.
line = file.readline()

-> readlines()
Reads all lines into a list.
lines = file.readlines()

with open("loan.txt", "r") as file:
    lines = file.readlines()
print(lines)

o/p:
[
    "Personal Loan\n",
    "Home Loan\n",
    "Car Loan\n",
    "Education Loan\n"
]
